      "The the placement lead owns the decision in availability change coverage; the preparer may compare, label, and route but may not approve the outcome. When urgency presses against the limit, pause and route the decision. A role change should trigger a review of queue access. Preparation, comparison, and follow-up may sit with the assistant. A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. The availability change coverage close note cites the placement record, the approver, and the time of the final check. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. If two roles share a queue, mark which one decides each item. Write the authority limit into the case template. The availability change coverage reviewer records client notice, the owner, and the next action in one place.",
      "## Evidence dictionary",
      "Each morning the team reviews availability change coverage arrivals, items waiting on the the placement lead, and items ready for a verified close. Record one next action and one due time per open item. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. Escalate an item that has waited past the written threshold. A sample availability change coverage review checks availability form, client schedule, and the surviving value in the placement record. A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. Record one next action and one due time per open item. Every availability change coverage handoff names the placement lead and the field in the placement record that will confirm the change.",
      "## Sampling and collection",
      "If the record does not match the surviving value, stop the dependent action and log the conflict in the placement record rather than choosing the more convenient value. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. A case that moves between owners should keep both owner periods visible. Do not let a deadline expand a role beyond its written limit. If the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. In this availability change coverage case, the record points to the placement record and names the placement lead as the decision owner. An escalation that ends in silence remains open. Check whether the exception came from a form, a rule, or a permission. Record who released the dependent action and when. For availability change coverage, compare availability form with the destination value rather than relying on a status label.",
      "## Analysis and reporting",
      "Record the availability change coverage close reason, the approver, and the surviving evidence reference in the same case note. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. Keep the prior value so the change can be explained. A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. Record the close reason with the same codes used in the exception queue. For availability change coverage, the working file keeps availability form and client schedule beside the decision note. The next reviewer should not have to ask which document is authoritative. Tie the close note to the original request and the final evidence. A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. The availability change coverage record should let a second reviewer rebuild the decision from client schedule and backup roster.",
      "## Limitations",
      "Review availability change coverage with a sample drawn from the queue export before the meeting, so the discussion cannot drift to memorable cases. End the review with one change and one measure. Report age and dependency, not only the total count. Report a null result as clearly as a positive one. Record the sample frame, the reviewer, and the criteria. The availability change coverage case note should show what the placement record held at the time and who reviewed it. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. The next reviewer should not have to ask which document is authoritative. Separate what was observed from what the team believes caused it. A availability change coverage exception keeps client notice attached and routes the question to the placement lead.",
      "## Review and next action",
      "The availability change coverage working paper should show the request, the source, the decision, the action, and the surviving value without a private inbox. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. Make the handoff readable by the next shift and the next auditor. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. Apply the same availability change coverage test to backup roster and to the value that survives in the placement record. Keep the source reference and the coded value in the same row. Name the owner and the date beside each decision. Make the handoff readable by the next shift and the next auditor. In the availability change coverage queue, an item without a next action is treated as an exception."
